      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Adding 0.5–2 wt% Y2O3 nanoparticles will improve the alloy's high-temperature creep resistance.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC8510135::web::026::4_2_characterization_of_the_rhea_bulks"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Adding Y2O3 nanoparticles will improve the irradiation resistance of the MoNbTaW-based alloy.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mechanical alloying followed by SPS at approximately 1150°C under a high-pressure inert atmosphere can consolidate the Y2O3-containing MoNbTaW-based composite.",
      "field": "intervention; conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5434025::web::007::introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Optimized milling parameters and possible particle surface treatments will produce a fine, uniform, sub-micron Y2O3 dispersion without substantial agglomeration.",
      "field": "intervention; structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Dispersed Y2O3 particles obstruct dislocation motion and thereby strengthen the alloy.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC8510135::web::026::4_2_characterization_of_the_rhea_bulks"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Y2O3 particles pin grain boundaries and stabilize the grain structure at high temperature.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC8510135::web::026::4_2_characterization_of_the_rhea_bulks"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Y2O3 particles act as irradiation-defect sinks that trap and promote recombination of radiation-induced point defects.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Y2O3-containing alloy will develop fewer irradiation-induced defect clusters than the monolithic baseline.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed mechanical and irradiation benefits will hold during testing at temperatures up to 900°C.",
      "field": "conditions; predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
